From 1d9ca564b29bb1f18bfd057b7f8319020bbae709 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ed <edimoldovan@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 12:11:36 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 10/15] ASoC: apple: t8140_aop_audio: drain the J714c sense RX
 for the whole speaker run

The T6050 speaker service's V/I sense comes back on its own RX DMA. Once
that RX goes undrained the firmware stops the speaker stream within about
0.2 s and does not deliver on it again, even to a restarted DMA, until the
service is restarted. So far the sense capture (speakersafetyd) owned that
DMA and the service ran only while the capture did: a daemon restart under
playback left the speakers silent until the next stream, and the amplifiers
lost their TDM clock with it.

Now the driver runs its own cyclic DMA on the RX for the whole run of the
speaker service, into a ring of 128 periods of 256 frames (0.68 s). The
sense capture has no DMA of its own: it reads the ring through the copy op
from a vmalloc buffer, its pointer following the drain's period count from
the capture's start. The DMA starts over at the ring's first byte on every
run of the drain, so a capture lagging behind at that moment reads one
block of the previous run's words.

The service follows playback alone: on the MCA serializer stream (T6050)
it starts from prepare, 20 ms before ASoC unmutes the amplifiers, which
fault on a missing TDM clock and stay down for the stream otherwise; it
stops from the trigger STOP work. Opening the sense capture no longer
sends pw0 to the speaker service.

CONFIG_I2C_CHARDEV in the j714c config: /dev/i2c-* for the i2c-tools reads
of the amplifiers.

Tested on J714c (-26 dBFS tones): speakersafetyd restarted 3 s into a 15 s
tone keeps the tone sounding and the sense data flowing; the daemon started
3 s into a stream starts sounding; plain playback after that; no daemon
panics; all six amplifiers deliver V/I through the ring.

[port to integration/aurora (aurora-j716s 6d9f1ec652a6): applied
 unchanged to sound/soc/apple/aop_t8140.rs, t8140_aop_audio.rs's name in
 this tree; DT and j714c.config hunks are board-specific and dropped]

